{
  "abstract": "A two-dimensional family of quaternionic Pryms contains an eightfold whose two orthogonal multiplicity systems are correlated with two genus-four Jacobians. Individual-factor Hodge conjectures do not establish the algebraicity of their mixed tensor. We construct it using two explicit dihedral correspondences between surfaces. The first leads from a quotient of a genus-29 curve squared to a surface with an elliptic Albanese pencil. A second degree-two function on the elliptic base gives a bigonal tower with rational norm whose partner is birational to the diagonal quaternion quotient of the genus-four curves. We verify the entire double-cover multiplier and descent involution, including its sign. The composite correspondence has transpose-composition four on the rank-sixteen inherited cohomology. Its full stabilizer and degree-one representations prove the rational and generalized Hodge conjectures on every power of the correlated product of the two fourfolds and the eightfold. After spreading, both conclusions hold for every pair in a fixed nonempty smooth parameter open, including all CM and source-isogeny loci. For two CM sources, their common quadratic centroid forces a dichotomy: independent Hodge tori or isogenous sources. The latter case has a disconnected preliminary stabilizer; actual Hodge homomorphisms identify the eightfold with the square of a source up to isogeny and remove the extra component. Exact coordinate, character-orbit and integral-lattice checks accompany the proof. Singular parameter boundaries and different quaternion algebras remain outside the result.",
  "author": "cm_symmetry_scout",
